<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hourly execution-metrics derivation (#1278, under #1272). Once an hour it
  derives one row for the last completed UTC hour and appends it to
  metrics.jsonl on the heartbeat branch (#1276). A second run over the same
  hour is idempotent, so a late or doubled fire does no harm.

  Why this exists: metrics.py derive has no other scheduler, and a row that
  is only derived by hand is as stale as whoever last remembered to run it
  while still reading as current.

  It reads the newest published snapshot (funnel.py snapshot, a local spool
  read) rather than running a live brief, so it spends no Projects GraphQL
  budget of its own; only the publisher runs brief.

  A Python script on a timer, not a headless prompt: AGENTS.md's
  in-app-scheduling rule covers Claude Code and Codex prompt execution and
  does not reach this, which is the same reading the publisher (#652) and the
  outcome derivation (#1288) already run under.

  StartCalendarInterval at minute 22, not StartInterval: the row is keyed to
  a clock hour, so the fire should be too. Minute 22 is off the Muse lanes'
  :00/:05/:15 slots and the outcome derivation's 03:20, and leaves the
  completed hour's last finishes time to reach the ledgers.

  The canonical copy lives here in the repo. launchd refuses a symlinked
  plist (`Bootstrap failed: 5: Input/output error`, measured 2026-09-07), so
  the installed file is a copy and tests/test_launchd_drift.py compares them.
  First install is scripts/install.sh plus a console bootstrap; after that
  the run-keeper refreshes it.

  Note for editors: XML forbids a double hyphen inside a comment. Use an em
  dash or a semicolon; plutil accepts the double hyphen and plistlib rejects
  it, so a file can lint clean and still be unparseable.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.nateprich.command-center-metrics-derive</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/usr/bin/python3</string>
        <string>/Users/nateprich/.claude/command-center-run/metrics.py</string>
        <string>derive</string>
    </array>

    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Minute</key>
        <integer>22</integer>
    </dict>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/nateprich/Library/Logs/command-center-metrics-derive.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/nateprich/Library/Logs/command-center-metrics-derive.err.log</string>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin:/Users/nateprich/.local/bin</string>
        <key>HOME</key>
        <string>/Users/nateprich</string>
    </dict>

    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Background</string>
</dict>
</plist>
